From 859c33a18413c348c8935918584d7183b535c0ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: licht <7687742+licht3345@user.noreply.gitee.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:02:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(export): support PyTorch < 2.6 hosts in the ONNX
 export path

The patched exporter targets PyTorch >= 2.6 (it passes dynamo=False to
torch.onnx.export and pins opset 20). PyTorch 2.2.2 is the final release with
an Intel macOS (x86_64) wheel, so those assumptions break four ways:

  1. transformers >= 4.54 refuses torch.load on .bin checkpoints unless
     torch >= 2.6 (CVE-2025-32434) -> add model.safetensors alongside.
  2. torch.onnx.export rejects the 'dynamo' kwarg on < 2.6 -> drop it.
  3. opset 20 is unsupported there; lowering to 19 emits legacy
     ReduceMean(axes=...) which only passes the checker up to opset 17.
     optimize_aio.py converts every artifact to opset 21 downstream, so the
     final bundle is unchanged.
  4. transformers defaults to SDPA attention, which the legacy exporter cannot
     translate -> force attn_implementation="eager" (mathematically identical).

Both compat steps are additive, idempotent, and only run when torch < 2.6, so
hosts on >= 2.6 behave exactly as before. The patch/GPT_SoVITS/ overlay is left
untouched; only the upstream clone copy is adapted, and 02_patch.sh restores it.

Verified by exporting v2ProPlus bundles for three voices (liuying, huahuo,
kafuka), each passing validate_bundle.sh --expect-v2pro and loading in
onnxruntime at opset 21.
